notes.content:
Now it is possible to play in 4 different modes:
- [b]Training[/b]: same as before, you play against a copy of your own deck and there's no prize;
- [b]Simple, normal or advanced match[/b], where you challenge an A.I. with gradually increasing difficulty and tougher decks, but you may win proportionally rare cards.

[h3]Better functions and aesthetics[/h3]
- You may now change your mind and come back after clicking on the "Comparison" button;
- Better decorations for menu, text boxes, points and selection indicators;
- Added an [b]options menu[/b], where you can modify the audio and image quality.

[h3]More intelligent A.I.[/h3]
Single player matches are going to be more interesting thanks to a massive improvement in the artificial intelligence algorithm. Now player 2 executes way more "logical" combos and also uses some special cards effects with more attention.

[h3]Many, many bugs solved[/h3]
Numerous game mechanics issues have been solved. The most important ones:
- Changing language makes the deck building menu unable to recognize previously saved cards;
- Automatic text messages are not translated when sent between users playing with different languages;
- "Pyromancer" sends an error while attempting to make you draw another card;
- "Magic Pumpkin" and "Clay Golem" can be eliminated by the "Lava Flow" effect although their text box states that they cannot be eliminated this way;
- Some cards like "Black Cat" or "Fearful Fairy" are not correctly eliminated after the resolution of their effects;
- Before the conclusion of a comparison certain cards are still targeted while they have already been eliminated by the effects of other cards during the same comparison;

[h3]Warning about your data![/h3]
Game files containing info about decks and personal profile, with the number of victories and the collected cards, now are encrypted. Because of this new method [b]older incompatible profile data will be cancelled[/b]!
